# Site rules (lavaforge.dev / obsidicore.com)
- Palette + type are LOCKED. Ember `#FF5B1F` is the single scarce accent; ember-on-dark button
  label is `#1a0d05`. Don't touch wordmark text or the sanctioned tokens.
- CSP / zero-JS is absolute: inline CSS or data: URIs only. No scripts, no external
  fonts/images/CDN. If an idea needs JS, it's out of scope.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is mandatory for any transform or looping animation; keep
  interactive transition durations <=250ms; name every transitioned property (never `all`).
- Lighthouse stays 100/100/100/100 (perf/bp/seo; lavaforge a11y is a pre-existing 95 from nav
  target-size). Composite-only animations (transform/opacity); no background-attachment:fixed;
  zero CLS (absolutely-positioned pseudo-elements).
- Coherence is a shared GESTURE, not a shared surface: lavaforge = warm build-log + ember
  horizon; obsidicore = cool glass slab + glint. Don't flatten one into the other.
- Deploy: `firebase deploy --only hosting` per project (needs the account that owns the
  Firebase project). Push source via the geoff-obsidicore token, not `gh auth switch`.
